    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Human settlements range from small <span class=\"learn-keyword\">villages</span> to large <span class=\"learn-keyword\">towns</span> and cities. Understanding the characteristics, similarities, and differences between towns and villages helps us study how human populations organise themselves in space.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Village</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A village is a small settlement with a relatively small population, usually engaged in primary activities (farming, fishing, forestry). Characteristics include:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Small population (typically fewer than 5,000 people).</li>\n  <li>Simple infrastructure — few roads, limited utilities.</li>\n  <li>Economy based on agriculture and fishing.</li>\n  <li>Close-knit community with strong social ties.</li>\n  <li>Few or no specialised services (hospitals, banks).</li>\n  <li>Low level of industrialisation.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Town</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A town is a larger settlement with a bigger population, more diverse economic activities, and better infrastructure. Characteristics include:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Larger population (typically 5,000–100,000 people).</li>\n  <li>More developed infrastructure (roads, hospitals, schools, markets).</li>\n  <li>Diverse economy — trade, services, light industry, administration.</li>\n  <li>Less personal community relations than a village.</li>\n  <li>Better access to utilities: electricity, pipe-borne water, internet.</li>\n  <li>Administrative functions (local government offices).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Similarities Between Towns and Villages</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Both are human settlements where people live.</li>\n  <li>Both have some form of administrative organisation.</li>\n  <li>Both have markets and commercial activities.</li>\n  <li>Both can grow in size over time.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Differences</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Village</th><th>Town</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Population</td><td>Small</td><td>Larger</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economy</td><td>Farming/fishing</td><td>Trade, industry, services</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Infrastructure</td><td>Basic/limited</td><td>More developed</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Services</td><td>Few</td><td>Many (hospitals, banks)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Community</td><td>Close-knit</td><td>Less personal</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Village = small, farming-based, close-knit community, limited services. Town = larger, diverse economy, better infrastructure, more services. Both are settlements with markets and can grow over time.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Villages: small population, farming economy, close-knit, limited infrastructure. Towns: larger population, diverse economy (trade + services), better infrastructure. Both are human settlements that can grow over time.\n</div>\n  ",
