    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Local Government Area (LGA)</span> is the third tier of government in Nigeria and the most basic unit of governance closest to the people. There are <span class=\"learn-keyword\">774 LGAs</span> in Nigeria. Understanding LGAs is important for studying the geographical organisation and administration of Nigeria.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Definition of LGA</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A Local Government Area (LGA) is a defined geographical and administrative unit of government responsible for local administration and service delivery to communities at the grassroots level.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Functions of the LGA</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Provision of primary health care and basic education.</li>\n  <li>Maintenance of roads and street lights at local level.</li>\n  <li>Provision of markets, parks, and recreational centres.</li>\n  <li>Registration of births, deaths, and marriages.</li>\n  <li>Collection of local taxes and rates.</li>\n  <li>Sanitation and waste management.</li>\n  <li>Agricultural extension services.</li>\n  <li>Construction and maintenance of drains.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of LGA in Geography</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>LGAs serve as the basic unit for geographical data collection (census, surveys).</li>\n  <li>They provide the framework for planning and development at the local level.</li>\n  <li>They help manage natural resources and the environment locally.</li>\n  <li>They enable students to study regional differences within states and Nigeria.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Structure of Government in Nigeria</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Level</th><th>Number</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>1st Tier</td><td>Federal Government</td><td>1</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>2nd Tier</td><td>State Government</td><td>36 states + FCT</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3rd Tier</td><td>Local Government Area (LGA)</td><td>774</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Nigeria has 774 LGAs. LGA is the 3rd tier (local/grassroots) government. Key functions: primary healthcare, basic education, roads, markets, sanitation, births/deaths registration. Kano State has the most LGAs (44); some states have fewer.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> 774 LGAs in Nigeria = 3rd tier government. Functions: healthcare, education, roads, markets, sanitation, tax collection. Importance in geography: data collection unit, local planning, resource management.\n</div>\n  ",
