    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Lowlands</span> are areas of relatively flat or gently undulating terrain close to sea level. They are among the most economically important landforms because they support dense populations, agriculture, and major settlements.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Types of Lowlands</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Plains:</strong> Flat, extensive areas of low-lying land. Examples: the Great Plains of North America, the Northern Plains of Nigeria.</li>\n  <li><strong>Plateaus:</strong> Elevated flat-topped landforms, often surrounded by escarpments. Examples: Jos Plateau (Nigeria), East African Plateau.</li>\n  <li><strong>River floodplains and deltas:</strong> Flat lands formed by river deposition. Example: Niger Delta (Nigeria).</li>\n  <li><strong>Coastal lowlands:</strong> Flat land along coastlines. Example: the coastal areas of Lagos and Cross River states.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Examples in Nigeria and West Africa</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Niger Delta:</strong> A vast lowland formed by river deposition; rich in oil and gas.</li>\n  <li><strong>Sokoto Plains:</strong> Low-lying areas in north-western Nigeria used for farming.</li>\n  <li><strong>Chad Basin:</strong> A lowland depression in north-eastern Nigeria.</li>\n  <li><strong>Coastal plains:</strong> Along the Atlantic coast from Nigeria to Senegal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of Lowlands</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Agriculture:</strong> Flat land is ideal for mechanised farming; fertile alluvial soils in floodplains.</li>\n  <li><strong>Settlements:</strong> Most of the world's major cities are built on lowlands due to ease of construction and accessibility.</li>\n  <li><strong>Transport:</strong> Roads and railways are easier and cheaper to build on flat land.</li>\n  <li><strong>Industry:</strong> Factory construction is easier and cheaper on flat ground.</li>\n  <li><strong>Trade:</strong> Coastal lowlands often have ports and harbours.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Lowland types: plains, plateaus, river floodplains/deltas, coastal lowlands. Nigerian examples: Niger Delta, Sokoto Plains, Chad Basin. Lowlands are important for agriculture, settlements, transport, and industry. Most major cities are on lowlands.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Lowlands = flat or gently undulating land near sea level. Types: plains, plateaus, floodplains, coastal. Nigerian examples: Niger Delta, Sokoto Plains, Chad Basin. Importance: farming, settlements, transport, industry, trade.\n</div>\n  ",
