    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">environment</span> is everything that surrounds us — both natural and human-made. It includes the air we breathe, the water we drink, the land we live on, and the societies we belong to. Understanding the environment and human interactions with it is central to geography.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Environment</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The environment refers to all living and non-living things surrounding an organism, including the physical, biological, social, and cultural conditions that influence its existence and development.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Components of the Environment</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Elements</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Physical (Natural) Environment</strong></td><td>Landforms, rocks, soils, water bodies, climate, vegetation, atmosphere</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Biological (Biotic) Environment</strong></td><td>Plants (flora), animals (fauna), micro-organisms</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Human (Social/Cultural) Environment</strong></td><td>Population, settlements, culture, religion, economy, government</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Interactions Between Humans and the Environment</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Humans and the environment constantly interact in two directions:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Environment influencing humans:</strong> Climate affects farming; terrain affects settlement; rivers provide water and transport.</li>\n  <li><strong>Humans influencing the environment:</strong> Deforestation, mining, agriculture, urbanisation, pollution — all modify the natural environment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Environmental Problems</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Deforestation — clearing forests for farming and logging.</li>\n  <li>Soil erosion — washing away of topsoil.</li>\n  <li>Air and water pollution — from industries, vehicles, and chemicals.</li>\n  <li>Desertification — encroachment of desert into productive land.</li>\n  <li>Flooding — from heavy rain, poor drainage, and deforestation.</li>\n  <li>Global warming/climate change — from increased greenhouse gases.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Three environment components: Physical (landforms, climate), Biological (plants, animals), Human/Social (culture, economy, settlements). Human-environment interaction is two-way: environment affects humans AND humans modify the environment. Key problems: deforestation, erosion, pollution, desertification.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Environment = all surroundings (living + non-living). Components: physical, biological, human. Interactions are two-way. Major problems: deforestation, erosion, pollution, desertification, flooding, climate change.\n</div>\n  ",
