    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Weather</span> refers to the atmospheric conditions of a place at a <span class=\"learn-keyword\">specific time</span>. It is what we experience day to day — sunshine, rain, wind, or clouds. Understanding weather is essential for agriculture, transport, aviation, and disaster preparedness.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Weather</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Weather is the state of the atmosphere at a particular place and time, including temperature, humidity, rainfall, wind, cloud cover, and sunshine. It can change from hour to hour or day to day.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Elements of Weather</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Definition</th><th>Instrument</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Temperature</td><td>Degree of hotness or coldness of the air</td><td>Thermometer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rainfall/Precipitation</td><td>Water falling from clouds as rain, snow, or hail</td><td>Rain gauge</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Humidity</td><td>Amount of water vapour in the air</td><td>Hygrometer/Psychrometer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Wind</td><td>Movement of air horizontally</td><td>Anemometer (speed); Wind vane (direction)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cloud cover</td><td>Amount of sky covered by clouds</td><td>Estimated in oktas (0–8)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sunshine</td><td>Amount of direct sunlight received</td><td>Sunshine recorder (Campbell-Stokes)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Atmospheric pressure</td><td>Weight of air pressing down on the Earth's surface</td><td>Barometer</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Weather vs. Climate</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>Weather</strong> = short-term atmospheric conditions (today's rain, this morning's temperature).</p>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>Climate</strong> = long-term average of weather over at least 30 years for a place.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance of Weather</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Guides farmers on when to plant and harvest.</li>\n  <li>Affects transportation and aviation safety.</li>\n  <li>Influences human clothing and shelter.</li>\n  <li>Early warning of storms and floods saves lives.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Weather = short-term (one day); Climate = long-term average (30 years). Key instruments: Thermometer (temperature), Rain gauge (rainfall), Anemometer (wind speed), Wind vane (wind direction), Barometer (pressure), Hygrometer (humidity), Campbell-Stokes recorder (sunshine).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Weather = atmospheric conditions at a specific time and place. Elements: temperature, rainfall, humidity, wind, cloud cover, sunshine, pressure. Measured with specific instruments. Weather differs from climate (climate = 30-year average).\n</div>\n  ",
