    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Nigeria is located in <span class=\"learn-keyword\">West Africa</span>, on the Gulf of Guinea. Its geographical position — straddling the tropics and having a long coastline — gives it a diverse climate, rich resources, and significant geopolitical importance.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Geographical Location</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Continent:</strong> Africa (West Africa).</li>\n  <li><strong>Latitudinal extent:</strong> 4°N to 14°N.</li>\n  <li><strong>Longitudinal extent:</strong> 3°E to 15°E.</li>\n  <li><strong>Area:</strong> Approximately 923,768 km².</li>\n  <li>Nigeria straddles the tropics — between the Equator and the Tropic of Cancer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Boundaries and Neighbours</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Direction</th><th>Boundary/Neighbour</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>North</td><td>Niger Republic and Chad Republic</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>East</td><td>Cameroon</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>West</td><td>Republic of Benin</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>South</td><td>Atlantic Ocean (Gulf of Guinea)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Significance of Nigeria's Location</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Strategic coastal location facilitates international trade through ports.</li>\n  <li>Location in the tropics provides warm climate suitable for diverse agriculture.</li>\n  <li>Bordering four countries promotes regional trade and diplomacy.</li>\n  <li>Coastal location in the Gulf of Guinea provides access to offshore oil resources.</li>\n  <li>Nigeria's size and location makes it a regional power in West Africa.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Nigeria's Position in Africa and the World</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Nigeria is Africa's most populous country (over 200 million people).</li>\n  <li>Nigeria is Africa's largest economy (by GDP).</li>\n  <li>Nigeria is a founding member of ECOWAS (Economic Community of West African States).</li>\n  <li>The Prime Meridian (0° longitude) passes through part of Nigeria at about 3–4°E, making Nigeria's time zone GMT+1.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Nigeria: 4°N–14°N latitude; 3°E–15°E longitude. Neighbours: Niger/Chad (N), Cameroon (E), Benin Republic (W), Atlantic Ocean (S). Area = ~923,768 km². Nigeria is in GMT+1 time zone. Most populous country in Africa.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Nigeria in West Africa: 4°N–14°N, 3°E–15°E, ~923,768 km². Bordered by Niger and Chad (N), Cameroon (E), Benin Republic (W), Atlantic Ocean (S). Africa's most populous country and largest economy. GMT+1.\n</div>\n  ",
