    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">map</span> is a representation of the Earth's surface on a flat surface. Map reading requires understanding <span class=\"learn-keyword\">scale</span>, <span class=\"learn-keyword\">direction</span>, <span class=\"learn-keyword\">symbols</span>, and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">conventional signs</span>.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Scale</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Statement scale:</strong> \"1 cm represents 1 km\".</li>\n  <li><strong>Representative Fraction (RF):</strong> 1:100,000 = 1 unit on map = 100,000 units on ground.</li>\n  <li><strong>Linear (graphical) scale:</strong> A bar divided into units on the map.</li>\n  <li>Large scale (e.g., 1:10,000) = small area, more detail.</li>\n  <li>Small scale (e.g., 1:1,000,000) = large area, less detail.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Direction and Bearing</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Four cardinal points: <strong>N, S, E, W</strong>. Four intermediate: NE, NW, SE, SW.</p>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>Bearing:</strong> Measured clockwise from North (000°–360°). E=090°; S=180°; W=270°.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Conventional Signs</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Symbol</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Main road</td><td>Double solid line</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Railway</td><td>Line with cross-hatch marks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>River</td><td>Blue wavy line</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Forest</td><td>Green shading or tree symbols</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contour lines</td><td>Brown lines of equal elevation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Large scale = more detail, smaller area. Small scale = less detail, larger area. E=090°, S=180°, W=270°, NW=315°. Railway = cross-hatch; river = blue wavy; contours = brown lines.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Scale (statement, RF, linear). Direction (N,S,E,W + bearings). Conventional signs represent real features. Contours = equal elevation lines.\n</div>\n  ",
