    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Map interpretation means reading <span class=\"learn-keyword\">physical features</span> (relief, drainage) and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">cultural features</span> (settlement, roads, land use) on topographic maps to understand the landscape.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Physical Features</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Relief:</strong> Steep = closely spaced contours. Flat = widely spaced.</li>\n  <li><strong>Hill:</strong> Concentric rings; higher values inside.</li>\n  <li><strong>Valley:</strong> V-shaped contours pointing upstream.</li>\n  <li><strong>Plateau:</strong> Wide flat top (wide contours) + steep edges (close contours).</li>\n  <li><strong>Rivers:</strong> Flow from high to low contour values (blue wavy lines).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Cultural Features</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Settlements: dots, names, or shaded built-up areas.</li>\n  <li>Roads: main = double line; minor = single; footpath = dotted.</li>\n  <li>Railways: line with cross-hatch marks.</li>\n  <li>Boundaries: dashed/dotted lines.</li>\n  <li>Forest: green shading or tree symbols.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Rivers flow HIGH → LOW contour values. V-shaped contours point UPSTREAM. Hill = concentric rings. Steep = closely spaced contours. Settlement on flat fertile valley = physical geography controls human activity.\n</div>\n  ",
